From: handheld-extra
Subject: [PATCH] steamcompmgr: keep the release point of a buffer with no scan-out FB

update_wayland_res() parks a commit's explicit-sync release point on the
buffer's scan-out FB, and drops it otherwise. A release point signals when it
is destroyed, so a buffer the display cannot scan out goes back to the client
the moment it is imported, before its frame is shown.

The Odin 3's display controller (Adreno 830 DPU) cannot scan out FP16
("Cannot import FB to DRM: format 0x48344258 and modifier 0x500000000000001
not supported for scan-out"), so every HDR (scRGB) frame hits this. With its
buffers handed back early the client is never held by FIFO: No Man's Sky kept
presenting ~60 fps under a 30 fps cap while ~750 of its frames queued in
gamescope, growing ~40/s, and the screen fell ever further behind
(AYN Odin 3, 2026-10-23). SDR, which gets an FB, was unaffected.

Keep the point with the commit when there is no FB, so it signals when the
commit is destroyed: the same lifetime as the commit's wlr_buffer lock.

Present in ValveSoftware and OpenGamingCollective gamescope as of 2026-10-23.

---
diff --git a/src/commit.h b/src/commit.h
--- a/src/commit.h
+++ b/src/commit.h
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@
 	bool ShouldPreemptivelyUpscale( GamescopeUpscaleFilter eFilter, GamescopeUpscaleScaler eScaler );
 
 	struct wlr_buffer *buf = nullptr;
+	// Explicit-sync release point for buffers without a scan-out FB to hold it.
+	std::shared_ptr<gamescope::CReleaseTimelinePoint> pReleasePoint;
 	gamescope::Rc<CVulkanTexture> vulkanTex;
 	std::optional<UpscaledTexture_t> upscaledTexture;
 
diff --git a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
--- a/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
+++ b/src/steamcompmgr.cpp
@@ -8647,6 +8647,13 @@
 		else
 			pBackendFb->SetBuffer( buf );
 	}
+	else
+	{
+		// No scan-out FB (e.g. an FP16 HDR buffer the display cannot scan out):
+		// a dropped release point signals at once, handing the client its buffer
+		// back before this frame is shown, and FIFO loses its back-pressure.
+		newCommit->pReleasePoint = std::move( reslistentry.pReleasePoint );
+	}
 
 	if ( eventFd != gamescope::CAcquireTimelinePoint::k_InvalidEvent )
 	{
-- 
